      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fenwick%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Surrounded by water on three sides, Fenwick evolved from a saltwater farm to a railroad‑connected enclave for Connecticut’s elite.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/CT/Middlesex_County/Fenwick_Borough.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Fenwick Historic District spans roughly 195 acres, includes 60 buildings, and joined the National Register of Historic Places in 1995.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fenwick%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Fenwick’s Inner and Outer Lighthouses guard the coast, with the Outer Light famously appearing on Connecticut license plates.",
